{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1787234987,"nonce":"VsAGt8Jf6ZN9tIGWhCySkdkTjW8=","message":"⛔ **Correction to this ticket's own premise, before anyone acts on it.** The title and body said\n\"every §C.7 key on the Case path carries `state_version` 1\". That is **too broad**. Verified:\n\n- `enqueueNotify` (`internal/alerts/service/service.go`) hard-codes `StateVersion: 1`, so every\n  evaluation **`alerts` enqueues** — `fired`, `acked`, `unacked`, `refired`, `resolved` — is pinned to\n  the literal 1. That half of the claim holds.\n- **Enrichment does not.** `NotifyEnriched` and `NotifyPreNotificationReady` leave the payload at `0`,\n  and `mint` (`internal/notification/service/notify.go:433`) treats a non-positive version as\n  *unpinned* and falls back to `Snapshot.Group.StateVersion` — which **is**\n  `alert_cases.state_version`, selected at `internal/notification/repository/snapshot.go:164`\n  (`o.state_version`) and scanned at `:645`. So an `enriched` evaluation already carries the real\n  optimistic lock.\n\nThe two producers agree at `fired` only by coincidence: a fresh Case's lock is the column's\n`DEFAULT 1`.\n\n⚠️ **And a comment in the tree states the opposite.** `internal/alerts/service/deps.go:286-288` reads\n*\"A Case carries no monotonic version, so every `enriched` evaluation for one Case now hashes\nIDENTICALLY forever\"*. Both halves are false — the column exists (`00023`, documented `00052`) and the\nenriched path reads it through `mint`'s fallback. That comment is being corrected separately.\n\n**What this changes about the work.** The defect is narrower and sharper than filed: it is not \"the\npin is absent\", it is **two producers of the same key disagree about how to supply its version**, and\nthe one that hard-codes is the one covering every human-visible lifecycle transition. Wiring\n`enqueueNotify` to read `Case.StateVersion()` would make the two agree rather than introduce something\nnew — which is a materially smaller change than the body implied, though it still re-keys those five\nreasons and so still wants the golden vector first.\n\nThe owner's ruling (stays hard-coded for now, recorded in SPEC §C.7) is unaffected and stands.","files":null}]}